WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.990
[MUSIC]

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.604
As foundations for nation states, religious nationalism and

00:00:08.604 --> 00:00:13.229
secular nationalism are often thought of as polar opposites.

00:00:13.229 --> 00:00:17.564
Those who value secular nationalism often depict religious

00:00:17.564 --> 00:00:22.579
nationalism as backward, irrational, repressive, and violent.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.270
In contrast, secular nationalism is depicted as modern,

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.150
rational, liberal, and peaceful.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.480
On the other hand, those who value religious nationalism often depict secular

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:43.550
nationalism as immoral, individual, and a vestige of colonialism.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.360
While religious nationalism is represented as moral, communal and

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.200
a form of self determination.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.650
All of these depictions perpetuate common misunderstandings of both religion and

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.500
secularism.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.030
In reality, religious nationalism and secular nationalism

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:08.600
are umbrella terms that include incredibly diverse ideologies.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.980
Their values can be overlapping or

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.150
in opposition, depending on social and historical context.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:20.360
For example, in 1923, the Republic of Turkey

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.760
was formed as a secular state, following the fall of the Ottoman Empire.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.640
It's first president, Kemal Ataturk brought in sweeping reforms that

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.120
replaced Muslim rule and culture, with a particular form of secularism.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:42.260
By the 1970s, Turkey was the most secular of all Muslim majority countries.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:47.290
But rampant inequality and the perception of government corruption gave rise to

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:54.270
Islamic parties that gained enough power by 1996 to form a coalition government.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.450
In response,

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:00.740
secular officials imposed a public ban on a symbol of Islam, the head scarf.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:07.270
Women who wore the hijab were no longer allowed to study at the university.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.520
And a democratically elected member of parliament named Merve Kavakci,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.850
representing the Islamic Virtue Party, was prevented

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:21.560
from taking the oath of office by her fellow secular National Assembly members.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.750
When she entered the parliament, they stood and yelled out for

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.500
30 minutes until she was forced to leave.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.330
Two weeks later, she was stripped of her Turkish citizenship.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:41.380
These and related restrictions emboldened members of Islamic political parties.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.660
And the current president, Recep Erdogan,

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.134
is an Islamist who has held power since 2003.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.250
In another example, the United States is a secular nation but

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.680
its currency is imprinted with, In God We Trust.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.340
The pledge of allegiance includes the phrase, one nation under God.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:10.710
And 42 of the 45 US presidents identified as Protestant Christians.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.570
India is also a secular nation but over the past few decades,

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:21.050
democratically elected Hindu nationalists have gained power.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.610
They enacted reforms in education and

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:29.260
culture that promote particular forms of Hinduism that many other Hindus and

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.380
members of other religious and secular communities find troubling.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:39.290
Like all world views, religious and secular forms of nationalism can

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:44.250
only be understood in their particular social and historical context.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.823
Understanding their rich diversities will enhance our understanding of

00:03:48.823 --> 00:03:52.518
movements on local, national and international levels.

